{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795697096,"nonce":"DSOoJtZG5mgNkOPKFP5PE/ydiqE=","title":"The media volume bar draws the set level dim and the rest bright","message":"In the controls of the media players, the columns up to the volume take --surface-elevated and the columns above it --text-secondary, so a muted player shows a bright full bar and a player at full volume a dim one. A muted bar also lights its first column, from the half column added to the threshold.\n\nSeen in the audio-player preview once the audio widget took these controls (the demo records muted).","files":null}]}